[32m+[m[32m# EmailTraceX[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEmailTraceX is a React/Vite/TypeScript frontend and FastAPI/SQLAlchemy backend for email security review and digital forensics. It includes demo dashboards as well as authenticated, organization-scoped account and email workflows.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Features[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Employee, SOC Analyst, and Organization Admin dashboards with server-assigned roles for authenticated sessions.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Argon2id password hashing, HttpOnly sessions, CSRF protection, invitations, and admin provisioning.[m
[32m+[m[32m- SOC Analyst `.eml` upload and complete raw-email paste modes. Both use the backend parser and save parsed records to the configured MySQL database.[m
[32m+[m[32m- An organization-scoped Investigation Queue that lists persisted email records and saved ML model assessments. Missing model results do not hide records.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Reproducible TF-IDF phishing-model training scripts, a bundled versioned model artifact, and test-only synthetic fixtures.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Existing demo views, charts, navigation, and review workflows remain available; demo data and model output are clearly distinct.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEmailTraceX does not visit extracted URLs or execute attachments. An ML result is an uncalibrated model assessment, not a confirmed security finding. Uploaded organization emails are not training data.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Requirements[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Node.js and npm (the lockfile is `package-lock.json`).[m
[32m+[m[32m- Python 3.11+ (see `backend/requirements.txt`).[m
[32m+[m[32m- MySQL 8+ for the authenticated application and MySQL integration tests.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Local setup[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mInstall the frontend dependencies from the project root:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32mnpm ci[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe backend reads the project-root `.env`. Preserve an existing `.env`; for a new checkout, copy the template only when no local file exists:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32mif (-not (Test-Path .env)) { Copy-Item backend\.env.example .env }[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSet a private MySQL `DATABASE_URL` that targets the intended EmailTraceX database. Do not commit `.env` or use production credentials for tests. From the project root, create and install a backend virtual environment:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32mpy -3 -m venv backend\.venv[m
[32m+[m[32mbackend\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1[m
[32m+[m[32mpython -m pip install -r backend\requirements.txt[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mInspect the configured database migration state without changing it:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32mSet-Location backend[m
[32m+[m[32mpython -m alembic current[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mDo not run migrations against an existing database unless the change is explicitly planned and approved. The current source tree includes an empty `0004_investigations.py` migration file, which causes Alembic to report that it cannot determine a revision ID. This cleanup does not modify migrations or the database. For first-time database setup, admin bootstrap, password recovery, invitation provisioning, and environment configuration, see [`backend/README.md`](backend/README.md).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mStart the backend from `backend\`:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32muvicorn app.main:app --reload --env-file ..\.env[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mStart the frontend in a second terminal from the project root:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32mnpm run dev[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe Vite development proxy sends `/api` requests to `http://127.0.0.1:8000` by default. Set `VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET` in the project-root `.env` to change the backend address.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Email model and dataset[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe deployed model is `backend/artifacts/phishing-email-v1.joblib`; accompanying metrics are in `backend/artifacts/phishing-email-v1.metrics.json`. The model artifact is retained as a versioned application resource. Large raw and processed training datasets are not committed; the setup script downloads and verifies the pinned public dataset. Training, evaluation, source/license, limitations, and exact commands are documented in [`backend/README.md`](backend/README.md).[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Tests and checks[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFrontend, from the project root:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32mnpm test[m
[32m+[m[32mnpm run typecheck[m
[32m+[m[32mnpm run lint[m
[32m+[m[32mnpm run build[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mBackend, from `backend\`, using an isolated temporary SQLite database:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32m$env:AUTH_TEST_SQLITE = "1"[m
[32m+[m[32mpython -m pytest -q[m
[32m+[m[32mRemove-Item Env:AUTH_TEST_SQLITE[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe backend suite can also use a dedicated MySQL test database via `AUTH_TEST_DATABASE_URL`. Its name must end in `_test`, and the schema must already be migrated. Tests use unique data and do not reset or truncate databases. Never point test settings at production.[m
[32m+[m
