[32m+[m[32m# EmailTraceX Authentication MVP[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis service provides Employee self-registration, email-bound SOC Analyst invitations, password login, server-managed sessions, session invalidation, current-user lookup, an authenticated test endpoint, and Organization Admin-only role provisioning. Public registration never grants privileged access.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Requirements and local setup[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Python 3.11 or newer[m
[32m+[m[32m- MySQL 8.0 or newer[m
[32m+[m[32m- Node.js/npm for the React frontend[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFrom the repository root, create a virtual environment and install backend dependencies:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32mpy -3 -m venv backend\.venv[m
[32m+[m[32mbackend\.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1[m
[32m+[m[32mpython -m pip install -r backend\requirements.txt[m
[32m+[m[32mif (-not (Test-Path .env)) { Copy-Item backend\.env.example .env }[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mCreate a MySQL database named `emailtracex` and a database account with access only to that database. Set `DATABASE_URL` and local settings in the project-root `.env` (the backend configuration loads this file); the URL format is `mysql+pymysql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:3306/DATABASE`. URL-encode special characters in the password. The `.env.example` values are placeholders, not usable credentials. Apply the schema and seed the default organization only when setting up a new database or after an explicitly approved migration:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32mSet-Location backend[m
[32m+[m[32malembic upgrade head[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mCreate the first organization administrator with an interactive password prompt:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32mpython create_admin.py[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIf the existing default-organization administrator has forgotten their password, run this local CLI from `backend\` using the database configuration in `.env`:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32mpython reset_admin_password.py --email admin@your-organization.example[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mEnter the new password and confirmation at the hidden prompts, then type `RESET ADMIN PASSWORD` when explicitly prompted. The command only resets the named account if it is already an Organization Admin in `DEFAULT_ORGANIZATION_ID`; it changes no roles or other users, and revokes that account's active sessions. It does not create an account or expose an HTTP recovery endpoint. Do not put a password in command-line arguments or environment variables.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mStart the API from `backend\`:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32muvicorn app.main:app --reload --env-file ..\.env[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIn a second terminal, start Vite from the repository root:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32mnpm run dev[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe Vite `/api` development proxy targets `http://127.0.0.1:8000` by default. Override `VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET` if needed. Generate a CSRF signing key before starting production:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```powershell[m
[32m+[m[32mpython -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(48))"[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mProduction must terminate HTTPS, set `COOKIE_SECURE=true`, use a unique `CSRF_SECRET` of at least 32 characters, configure exact `ALLOWED_ORIGINS`, use `SameSite=Lax` or stricter, and proxy `/api` to the backend over a protected network. Keep `.env` private. Development generates a process-local CSRF key when none is set.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Environment variables[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mSee `backend/.env.example` for the template used to create the project-root `.env`. Vite reads `VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET` from that same root environment file; no separate frontend environment template is required. `DATABASE_URL` should use MySQL with the `mysql+pymysql` driver. `DEFAULT_ORGANIZATION_ID` must match the default organization seeded by migration `0001_auth_schema` (or a future organization-specific migration). Session tokens are random opaque values; only SHA-256 token digests are stored in the database. CSRF tokens are held in an in-memory frontend request flow and a SameSite cookie, never in localStorage.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## API[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- `GET /api/auth/csrf` issues a CSRF cookie and returns its value.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `POST /api/auth/register` accepts `full_name`, `email`, and a password of at least 8 characters (maximum 1,024 UTF-8 bytes); rejects extra fields and creates Employee only.[m
[32m+[m[32m- `POST /api/auth/register/invited` accepts registration details and an invitation token; consumes a valid, email-bound SOC 